{"t":"2026-05-28T03:39:58.484Z","event":"sdk_msg","msg":{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-5-20251101","id":"msg_01GC159jiHNyhgyCnn22Ckvr","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_019Mh899LZyG7Q7ErLoWvBHp","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/Users/spy/mfautomations/repos/creation-station/reverse-search/synthetics/fixtures/candidates.yaml","content":"# Copyright 2026 VibeSpace LLC\n# Licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0\n#\n# Synthetic Candidate Fixtures for Drift Detection\n# =================================================\n# These candidates exercise the Discovery -> Score pipeline with known inputs.\n# UUIDs are derived via uuid5(NAMESPACE_DNS, \"synthetic-{slug}\") per NUTRIENTS.md I.1\n\ncandidates:\n  - slug: synthetic-jr-engineer\n    name: Jordan Rivera\n    email: synthetic-jr-engineer@talent-agent.test\n    linkedin_url: https://linkedin.com/in/synthetic-jr-engineer\n    github_url: https://github.com/synthetic-jr-engineer\n    target_locations:\n      - New York, NY\n      - Brooklyn, NY\n    remote_preference: hybrid\n    min_compensation: 80000\n    excluded_companies:\n      - Acme Corp\n    excluded_industries:\n      - Defense\n    personal_context: |\n      Recent bootcamp graduate with a passion for building user-facing products.\n      Looking for mentorship opportunities at a growth-stage company.\n      Interested in fintech and developer tools.\n    resume_text: |\n      JORDAN RIVERA\n      Full-Stack Software Engineer\n      New York, NY | jordan.rivera@email.com | github.com/synthetic-jr-engineer\n\n      SUMMARY\n      Entry-level full-stack developer with 1.5 years of experience building web applications.\n      Strong foundation in React, TypeScript, and Node.js. Passionate about clean code,\n      user experience, and continuous learning. Seeking opportunities at innovative companies\n      where I can contribute to meaningful products while growing as an engineer.\n\n      TECHNICAL SKILLS\n      Languages: JavaScript, TypeScript, Python, SQL\n      Frontend: React, Next.js, HTML5, CSS3, Tailwind CSS\n      Backend: Node.js, Express, FastAPI\n      Databases: PostgreSQL, MongoDB, Redis\n      Tools: Git, Docker, AWS (S3, EC2), Vercel, GitHub Actions\n      Testing: Jest, React Testing Library, Cypress\n\n      EXPERIENCE\n\n      Junior Software Engineer | TechStart Inc. | Jun 2024 - Present\n      - Built and maintained React components for customer-facing dashboard serving 10K+ users\n      - Implemented RESTful API endpoints using Node.js and Express\n      - Reduced page load time by 40% through code splitting and lazy loading\n      - Collaborated with senior engineers on database schema design\n      - Participated in code reviews and agile ceremonies\n\n      Software Engineering Intern | WebFlow Agency | Jan 2024 - May 2024\n      - Developed responsive landing pages for 5+ client projects\n      - Created reusable component library reducing development time by 25%\n      - Integrated third-party APIs including Stripe and SendGrid\n      - Wrote unit tests achieving 80% code coverage\n\n      PROJECTS\n\n      TaskFlow (Personal Project) | github.com/synthetic-jr-engineer/taskflow\n      - Full-stack task management app with React, Node.js, PostgreSQL\n      - Implemented real-time updates using WebSockets\n      - Deployed on AWS with CI/CD pipeline\n\n      CodeBuddy (Hackathon Winner) | 2nd Place, NYC Hackathon 2024\n      - AI-powered code review assistant using OpenAI API\n      - Built Chrome extension with 500+ downloads\n\n      EDUCATION\n\n      Full-Stack Web Development Certificate | Coding Academy NYC | 2023\n      Bachelor of Science, Computer Science | State University | 2023\n      - GPA: 3.6/4.0\n      - Relevant coursework: Data Structures, Algorithms, Database Systems\n\n      CERTIFICATIONS\n      - AWS Cloud Practitioner (2024)\n      - Meta Front-End Developer Certificate (2023)\n\n  - slug: synthetic-senior-ml\n    name: Dr. Samantha Chen\n    email: synthetic-senior-ml@talent-agent.test\n    linkedin_url: https://linkedin.com/in/synthetic-senior-ml\n    github_url: https://github.com/synthetic-senior-ml\n    target_locations:\n      - San Francisco, CA\n      - Remote\n    remote_preference: remote_only\n    min_compensation: 250000\n    excluded_companies:\n      - Meta\n      - Oracle\n    excluded_industries:\n      - Oil & Gas\n      - Tobacco\n    personal_context: |\n      Staff ML engineer with deep experience in recommendation systems and NLP.\n      Looking for a role where I can lead technical direction for ML infrastructure.\n      Interested in AI safety and responsible AI development.\n    resume_text: |\n      DR. SAMANTHA CHEN\n      Staff Machine Learning Engineer\n      San Francisco, CA | samantha.chen@email.com | github.com/synthetic-senior-ml\n\n      SUMMARY\n      Staff-level machine learning engineer with 8+ years of experience building production ML\n      systems at scale. PhD in Computer Science with focus on deep learning and NLP.\n      Track record of leading cross-functional teams, mentoring engineers, and delivering\n      high-impact ML products. Expertise in recommendation systems, large language models,\n      and MLOps infrastructure.\n\n      TECHNICAL SKILLS\n      ML Frameworks: PyTorch, TensorFlow, JAX, Hugging Face Transformers\n      Infrastructure: Kubernetes, Ray, Spark, Airflow, MLflow, Weights & Biases\n      Cloud: AWS (SageMaker, EKS, S3), GCP (Vertex AI, BigQuery), Azure ML\n      Languages: Python, C++, Rust, SQL\n      Specializations: Recommendation Systems, NLP, Computer Vision, Distributed Training\n\n      EXPERIENCE\n\n      Staff Machine Learning Engineer | AI Dynamics | Mar 2021 - Present\n      - Lead ML platform team of 6 engineers building recommendation infrastructure\n      - Architected distributed training pipeline reducing model training time by 70%\n      - Designed and deployed real-time recom