{"t":"2026-05-28T03:40:38.663Z","event":"sdk_msg","msg":{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-5-20251101","id":"msg_01YUDFkd4jpzPMwtDcYdtG2B","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The directory is empty. Now I'll create all 12 JD files:"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":212,"cache_read_input_tokens":78669,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":212,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"115930cd-9f87-4632-b47e-ed08593aff21","uuid":"b07c9e2e-0348-43b1-ae52-bf0556a61a4a"}}
{"t":"2026-05-28T03:40:49.823Z","event":"sdk_msg","msg":{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-5-20251101","id":"msg_01YUDFkd4jpzPMwtDcYdtG2B","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_019neJ4mUtju51JH7i2UHbrd","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/Users/spy/mfautomations/repos/creation-station/reverse-search/synthetics/fixtures/jobs/jr-01-strong-swe.md","content":"---\n# Copyright 2026 VibeSpace LLC\n# Licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0\n#\n# JD Fixture: Strong match for synthetic-jr-engineer\n# Contract: NUTRIENTS.md I.9 SyntheticJobFixture\n\ntarget_candidate: synthetic-jr-engineer\nexpected_hot: true\nexpected_score_band: high\nsource: greenhouse\n---\n\n# Junior Full-Stack Engineer\n\n**Company:** TechFlow Inc.\n**Location:** New York, NY (Hybrid - 2 days/week in office)\n**Salary:** $85,000 - $105,000\n\n## About Us\n\nTechFlow is a fast-growing fintech startup building the future of expense management for small businesses. We're backed by top-tier VCs and serve over 50,000 customers. Our engineering team values clean code, continuous learning, and shipping features that make a real difference.\n\n## The Role\n\nWe're looking for a Junior Full-Stack Engineer to join our product team. You'll work closely with senior engineers to build and maintain our React-based dashboard and Node.js backend. This is a great opportunity to grow your skills while contributing to a product used by thousands of businesses daily.\n\n## What You'll Do\n\n- Build responsive React components for our customer-facing dashboard\n- Develop RESTful API endpoints using Node.js and Express\n- Write unit and integration tests to ensure code quality\n- Participate in code reviews and learn from experienced engineers\n- Collaborate with designers to implement beautiful, accessible UIs\n- Help maintain our PostgreSQL database and optimize queries\n\n## What We're Looking For\n\n- 1-2 years of experience with JavaScript/TypeScript\n- Proficiency with React and modern frontend development\n- Experience building backend services with Node.js\n- Familiarity with PostgreSQL or similar relational databases\n- Understanding of Git and version control best practices\n- Strong communication skills and eagerness to learn\n\n## Nice to Have\n\n- Experience with testing frameworks (Jest, Cypress)\n- Familiarity with Docker and CI/CD pipelines\n- Interest in fintech or developer tools\n- Contributions to open-source projects\n\n## Benefits\n\n- Competitive salary + equity\n- Health, dental, and vision insurance\n- Unlimited PTO\n- $1,500 annual learning budget\n- Remote-friendly with flexible hours\n- Monthly team events\n\nTechFlow is an equal opportunity employer. We celebrate diversity and are committed to creating an inclusive environment for all employees.\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":212,"cache_read_input_tokens":78669,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":212,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"115930cd-9f87-4632-b47e-ed08593aff21","uuid":"b07c96af-3b0c-4e82-8bbe-7e4b786c537f"}}
{"t":"2026-05-28T03:40:58.381Z","event":"sdk_msg","msg":{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-5-20251101","id":"msg_01YUDFkd4jpzPMwtDcYdtG2B","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01NXuiSaHhkNSn8CDjx6wQ1V","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/Users/spy/mfautomations/repos/creation-station/reverse-search/synthetics/fixtures/jobs/jr-02-strong-fullstack.md","content":"---\n# Copyright 2026 VibeSpace LLC\n# Licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0\n#\n# JD Fixture: Strong variant match for synthetic-jr-engineer\n# Contract: NUTRIENTS.md I.9 SyntheticJobFixture\n\ntarget_candidate: synthetic-jr-engineer\nexpected_hot: true\nexpected_score_band: high\nsource: lever\n---\n\n# Software Engineer I - Full Stack\n\n**Company:** DevPortal\n**Location:** Brooklyn, NY (Hybrid)\n**Salary:** $80,000 - $100,000 + equity\n\n## About DevPortal\n\nDevPortal is building the world's best developer documentation platform. We help engineering teams create beautiful, searchable docs that developers actually want to read. Used by companies like Stripe, Vercel, and Notion.\n\n## The Role\n\nJoin our small but mighty engineering team as a Software Engineer I. You'll have the opportunity to work across our entire stack, from our Next.js frontend to our Python backend. We believe in giving engineers ownership and the chance to learn rapidly.\n\n## Responsibilities\n\n- Ship features end-to-end, from database to UI\n- Build React components with TypeScript for our web application\n- Develop APIs using FastAPI and PostgreSQL\n- Write tests and documentation for new features\n- Participate in architecture discussions and code reviews\n- Debug production issues and improve system reliability\n\n## Requirements\n\n- 1-3 years of software development experience\n- Strong JavaScript/TypeScript skills\n- Experience with React or similar frontend frameworks\n- Backend development experience (Node.js, Python, or similar)\n- Comfortable with SQL databases\n- Self-motivated learner who thrives in ambiguity\n\n## Bonus Points\n\n- Experience with Next.js or server-side rendering\n- Knowledge of search technologies (Elasticsearch, Algolia)\n- Background in developer tools or documentation\n- Open source contributions\n\n## What We Offer\n\n- Competitive base salary + meaningful equity\n- Hybrid work: 3 days remote, 2 days in our Brooklyn office\n- Premium health benefits\n- $2,000 home office stipend\n- Conference attendance budget\n- Weekly team lunches and monthly outings\n\n## Our Stack\n\nFrontend: React, Next.js, TypeScript, Tailwind CSS\nBackend: FastAPI, Python, PostgreSQL, Redis\nInfrastructure: Vercel, AWS, Docker\n\nApply now and help us build the future of developer documentation!\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":212,"cache_read_input_tokens":78669,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":212,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"115930cd-9f87-4632-b47e-ed08593aff21","uuid":"f9220e66-8ab5-451e-b872-e71aa0c2e11c"}}
{"t":"2026-05-28T03:41:08.409Z","event":"sdk_msg","msg":{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-5-20251101","id":"msg_01YUDFkd4jpzPMwtDcYdtG2B","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01TJ8Cnz6n258gph3vU19ynm","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/Users/spy/mfautomations/repos/creation-station/reverse-search/synthetics/fixtures/jobs/jr-03-weak-devops.md","content":"---\n# Copyright 2026 VibeSpace LLC\n# Licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0\n#\n# JD Fixture: Weak match for synthetic-jr-engineer (DevOps role, different focus)\n# Contract: NUTRIENTS.md I.9 SyntheticJobFixture\n\ntarget_candidate: synthetic-jr-engineer\nexpected_hot: false\nexpected_score_band: low\nsource: ashby\n---\n\n# Junior DevOps Engineer\n\n**Company:** CloudScale Solutions\n**Location:** Chicago, IL (On-site required)\n**Salary:** $75,000 - $95,000\n\n## About CloudScale\n\nCloudScale Solutions is a managed services provider helping mid-market companies migrate to and operate in the cloud. We manage infrastructure for over 200 clients across AWS, GCP, and Azure.\n\n## Role Overview\n\nWe're seeking a Junior DevOps Engineer to join our infrastructure team. You'll focus on maintaining client cloud environments, automating deployments, and ensuring 24/7 system reliability. This is a hands-on role for someone passionate about infrastructure and operations.\n\n## Key Responsibilities\n\n- Monitor and maintain production Kubernetes clusters\n- Write Terraform and Ansible scripts for infrastructure automation\n- Respond to production incidents and participate in on-call rotation\n- Configure and manage CI/CD pipelines using Jenkins and GitLab CI\n- Implement security best practices and compliance requirements\n- Document infrastructure changes and runbooks\n- Assist with client onboarding and migrations\n\n## Requirements\n\n- 1-2 years of experience in DevOps, SRE, or systems administration\n- Strong Linux administration skills (Ubuntu, CentOS)\n- Experience with containerization (Docker, Kubernetes)\n- Familiarity with Infrastructure as Code (Terraform, CloudFormation)\n- Understanding of networking concepts (TCP/IP, DNS, load balancing)\n- Scripting skills in Bash, Python, or Go\n- AWS or GCP certification preferred\n\n## Nice to Have\n\n- Experience with monitoring tools (Datadog, Prometheus, Grafana)\n- Knowledge of security tools and practices\n- Database administration experience (MySQL, PostgreSQL)\n- Previous MSP or consulting experience\n\n## What We Offer\n\n- Base salary + performance bonus\n- Health and dental insurance\n- 401(k) with 4% match\n- Professional development budget\n- On-call compensation\n- Path to senior roles within 2 years\n\n## Schedule\n\n- Monday-Friday, 9 AM - 5 PM CT\n- On-call rotation every 4 weeks\n- Some weekend work during maintenance windows\n\nThis is an on-site position at our Chicago headquarters. Remote work is not available for this role.\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":212,"cache_read_input_tokens":78669,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":212,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"115930cd-9f87-4632-b47e-ed08593aff21","uuid":"838709a9-ff07-437a-92f1-c55444a6bce8"}}
