{"t":"2026-05-28T03:41:20.200Z","event":"sdk_msg","msg":{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-5-20251101","id":"msg_013DfdCyfTk1Sk7sieYUU8ga","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Now let me create the ML engineer JDs:"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2937,"cache_read_input_tokens":78881,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":2937,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":6,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"115930cd-9f87-4632-b47e-ed08593aff21","uuid":"3806fa75-0065-4c4d-a72f-278815f6e972"}}
{"t":"2026-05-28T03:41:32.313Z","event":"sdk_msg","msg":{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-5-20251101","id":"msg_013DfdCyfTk1Sk7sieYUU8ga","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01FMM7CwGYzgspEB8h4Pkqrs","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/Users/spy/mfautomations/repos/creation-station/reverse-search/synthetics/fixtures/jobs/ml-01-strong-staff.md","content":"---\n# Copyright 2026 VibeSpace LLC\n# Licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0\n#\n# JD Fixture: Strong match for synthetic-senior-ml\n# Contract: NUTRIENTS.md I.9 SyntheticJobFixture\n\ntarget_candidate: synthetic-senior-ml\nexpected_hot: true\nexpected_score_band: high\nsource: greenhouse\n---\n\n# Staff Machine Learning Engineer - LLM Infrastructure\n\n**Company:** Nexus AI\n**Location:** San Francisco, CA (Remote OK)\n**Salary:** $280,000 - $350,000 + equity\n\n## About Nexus AI\n\nNexus AI is building the next generation of AI infrastructure. Our platform powers some of the world's most demanding ML workloads, from training foundation models to serving billions of inference requests daily. Backed by $200M in Series C funding, we're growing rapidly and looking for exceptional talent.\n\n## The Role\n\nWe're looking for a Staff Machine Learning Engineer to lead technical direction for our LLM infrastructure team. You'll architect and build systems that train and serve large language models at massive scale, working alongside world-class researchers and engineers.\n\n## What You'll Do\n\n- Lead technical design for distributed training infrastructure supporting 1000+ GPU clusters\n- Architect efficient inference systems for LLMs with strict latency requirements\n- Drive adoption of best practices for MLOps, experiment tracking, and model versioning\n- Mentor a team of 5-8 ML engineers, fostering technical growth and excellence\n- Collaborate with research teams to productionize novel architectures\n- Publish technical blogs and represent the company at conferences\n- Contribute to open-source ML tooling and infrastructure projects\n\n## Requirements\n\n- 8+ years of experience in machine learning engineering\n- Deep expertise in PyTorch, distributed training (FSDP, DeepSpeed), and GPU optimization\n- Experience building production ML systems serving millions of users\n- Strong understanding of transformer architectures and attention mechanisms\n- Track record of leading technical initiatives and mentoring engineers\n- MS or PhD in Computer Science, Machine Learning, or related field\n- Published research in top-tier venues (NeurIPS, ICML, ICLR) preferred\n\n## Our Stack\n\n- Training: PyTorch, JAX, CUDA, Ray, Slurm\n- Inference: vLLM, TensorRT, Triton, Kubernetes\n- Infrastructure: AWS, GCP, custom on-prem clusters\n- Observability: Weights & Biases, Prometheus, Grafana\n\n## Benefits\n\n- Top-of-market compensation + generous equity\n- Premium health, dental, and vision coverage\n- $10,000 annual learning and conference budget\n- Flexible remote work with optional SF office access\n- Compute credits for personal research projects\n- Regular team offsites and company events\n\n## Why Join Us?\n\nYou'll work on some of the most challenging ML infrastructure problems in the industry, with access to massive compute resources and brilliant colleagues. If you're excited about pushing the boundaries of what's possible with large language models, we want to talk.\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2937,"cache_read_input_tokens":78881,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":2937,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":6,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"115930cd-9f87-4632-b47e-ed08593aff21","uuid":"70f565db-f8a7-43ad-90f3-139241d79a5d"}}
{"t":"2026-05-28T03:41:41.208Z","event":"sdk_msg","msg":{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-5-20251101","id":"msg_013DfdCyfTk1Sk7sieYUU8ga","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_014RRbxYgDudgpRU8uupKHrH","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/Users/spy/mfautomations/repos/creation-station/reverse-search/synthetics/fixtures/jobs/ml-02-strong-research.md","content":"---\n# Copyright 2026 VibeSpace LLC\n# Licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0\n#\n# JD Fixture: Strong variant match for synthetic-senior-ml (Research focus)\n# Contract: NUTRIENTS.md I.9 SyntheticJobFixture\n\ntarget_candidate: synthetic-senior-ml\nexpected_hot: true\nexpected_score_band: high\nsource: lever\n---\n\n# Senior Research Engineer - ML Systems\n\n**Company:** DeepMind\n**Location:** Remote (US)\n**Salary:** $300,000 - $400,000 + equity\n\n## About the Role\n\nDeepMind is seeking a Senior Research Engineer to bridge the gap between cutting-edge research and production systems. You'll work closely with researchers to implement and scale novel ML algorithms, contributing to breakthroughs in AI capability and safety.\n\n## What You'll Do\n\n- Implement research prototypes and scale them to production quality\n- Optimize training and inference pipelines for efficiency\n- Design distributed systems for large-scale experiments\n- Contribute to research papers and open-source releases\n- Collaborate with researchers to identify engineering solutions to research problems\n- Build tools and infrastructure that accelerate the research-to-production cycle\n- Participate in technical architecture decisions and code reviews\n\n## Requirements\n\n- 7+ years of experience in ML engineering or applied research\n- Expert-level Python and experience with ML frameworks (PyTorch, JAX, TensorFlow)\n- Strong background in distributed systems and parallel computing\n- Experience with GPU programming (CUDA) and optimization\n- Track record of shipping ML systems at scale\n- Excellent communication skills for cross-functional collaboration\n- PhD or equivalent research experience in ML/AI preferred\n\n## Desired Qualifications\n\n- Publications at major ML conferences\n- Experience with reinforcement learning systems\n- Background in NLP or computer vision\n- Contributions to popular ML libraries\n- Experience with TPU programming\n\n## Compensation & Benefits\n\n- Highly competitive salary and equity\n- Comprehensive health coverage\n- Generous parental leave\n- Annual research budget\n- Flexible work arrangements\n- Publication and conference support\n- Access to world-class compute infrastructure\n\n## About DeepMind\n\nDeepMind is one of the world's leading AI research companies, with a mission to solve intelligence and use it to benefit humanity. Our team has made breakthrough contributions to deep learning, reinforcement learning, and AI safety.\n\nJoin us in pushing the boundaries of AI research while ensuring its benefits are broadly shared.\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2937,"cache_read_input_tokens":78881,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":2937,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":6,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"115930cd-9f87-4632-b47e-ed08593aff21","uuid":"6fb06600-9682-44aa-a4c1-f77e628bc57c"}}
{"t":"2026-05-28T03:41:50.564Z","event":"sdk_msg","msg":{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-5-20251101","id":"msg_013DfdCyfTk1Sk7sieYUU8ga","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01FsbUiBCi9KyqVsMERcUyTZ","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/Users/spy/mfautomations/repos/creation-station/reverse-search/synthetics/fixtures/jobs/ml-03-weak-junior.md","content":"---\n# Copyright 2026 VibeSpace LLC\n# Licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0\n#\n# JD Fixture: Weak match for synthetic-senior-ml (Junior level, underqualified)\n# Contract: NUTRIENTS.md I.9 SyntheticJobFixture\n\ntarget_candidate: synthetic-senior-ml\nexpected_hot: false\nexpected_score_band: low\nsource: ashby\n---\n\n# Junior Machine Learning Engineer\n\n**Company:** DataStart Analytics\n**Location:** Austin, TX (On-site)\n**Salary:** $85,000 - $110,000\n\n## About Us\n\nDataStart Analytics is a growing data science consultancy helping small and medium businesses leverage machine learning. We work across industries including retail, healthcare, and finance.\n\n## The Role\n\nWe're looking for a Junior Machine Learning Engineer to join our team. You'll work under the guidance of our senior data scientists to build and deploy ML models for client projects.\n\n## Responsibilities\n\n- Develop predictive models using scikit-learn and basic deep learning\n- Clean and preprocess datasets for analysis\n- Create visualizations and reports for client presentations\n- Assist with model deployment using Flask and Docker\n- Document code and methodologies\n- Participate in client meetings and gather requirements\n\n## Requirements\n\n- Bachelor's degree in Computer Science, Statistics, or related field\n- 0-2 years of experience in data science or machine learning\n- Proficiency in Python and SQL\n- Familiarity with scikit-learn, pandas, and numpy\n- Basic understanding of statistical concepts\n- Good communication skills\n\n## Nice to Have\n\n- Experience with cloud platforms (AWS, GCP)\n- Knowledge of deep learning frameworks\n- Prior consulting or client-facing experience\n- Master's degree in a quantitative field\n\n## What We Offer\n\n- Competitive salary for entry-level role\n- Health insurance\n- 401(k) plan\n- Mentorship from senior data scientists\n- Exposure to diverse industries and problems\n- Professional development opportunities\n\n## Our Tech Stack\n\n- Languages: Python, SQL\n- ML: scikit-learn, XGBoost, basic TensorFlow\n- Tools: Jupyter, Git, Docker basics\n- Cloud: AWS (learning supported)\n\nThis is an entry-level position. Candidates with extensive experience should apply for our Senior Data Scientist role instead.\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2937,"cache_read_input_tokens":78881,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":2937,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":6,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"115930cd-9f87-4632-b47e-ed08593aff21","uuid":"3af98cbb-9ba8-4f08-8375-9d868ab9510a"}}
{"t":"2026-05-28T03:41:57.782Z","event":"sdk_msg","msg":{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-5-20251101","id":"msg_013DfdCyfTk1Sk7sieYUU8ga","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_016aphaXK8L3A8iTUhk4FrX5","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/Users/spy/mfautomations/repos/creation-station/reverse-search/synthetics/fixtures/jobs/ml-04-mismatch-pm.md","content":"---\n# Copyright 2026 VibeSpace LLC\n# Licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0\n#\n# JD Fixture: Mismatch for synthetic-senior-ml (Product Manager role, wrong domain)\n# Contract: NUTRIENTS.md I.9 SyntheticJobFixture\n\ntarget_candidate: synthetic-senior-ml\nexpected_hot: false\nexpected_score_band: low\nsource: greenhouse\n---\n\n# Product Manager - AI Platform\n\n**Company:** TechCorp Industries\n**Location:** Seattle, WA (Hybrid)\n**Salary:** $150,000 - $200,000\n\n## About TechCorp\n\nTechCorp Industries is a Fortune 500 technology company building enterprise software solutions. Our AI Platform team develops tools that help businesses automate workflows using machine learning.\n\n## The Role\n\nWe're seeking a Product Manager to lead our AI Platform product line. You'll define product strategy, work with customers, and drive the roadmap for our ML tooling products.\n\n## Responsibilities\n\n- Define product vision and strategy for the AI Platform\n- Conduct customer research and gather market requirements\n- Write detailed PRDs and user stories for engineering teams\n- Prioritize features based on business impact and customer needs\n- Collaborate with engineering, design, and sales teams\n- Present product updates to executive leadership\n- Analyze product metrics and drive continuous improvement\n- Manage product launches and go-to-market activities\n\n## Requirements\n\n- 5+ years of product management experience\n- Experience with AI/ML products or enterprise software\n- Strong analytical and problem-solving skills\n- Excellent communication and presentation abilities\n- MBA or equivalent business experience preferred\n- Technical background helpful but not required\n- Experience with Agile methodologies\n\n## What We're NOT Looking For\n\nThis is a product management role, not a hands-on engineering position. Candidates seeking to write code or build ML models should explore our engineering openings instead.\n\n## Benefits\n\n- Competitive base salary + annual bonus\n- Comprehensive health benefits\n- 401(k) with company match\n- Stock purchase program\n- Generous PTO policy\n- Professional development budget\n\n## About the Team\n\nOur AI Platform team consists of 25 engineers, 3 designers, and 2 product managers. We ship quarterly releases and iterate based on customer feedback. The successful candidate will own the roadmap for our model deployment and monitoring tools.\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2937,"cache_read_input_tokens":78881,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":2937,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":2684,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"115930cd-9f87-4632-b47e-ed08593aff21","uuid":"41f1ce14-d279-4209-93dd-50cde6c71d7b"}}
{"t":"2026-05-28T03:41:57.796Z","event":"sdk_msg","msg":{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01FMM7CwGYzgspEB8h4Pkqrs","type":"tool_result","content":"File created successfully at: /Users/spy/mfautomations/repos/creation-station/reverse-search/synthetics/fixtures/jobs/ml-01-strong-staff.md"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"115930cd-9f87-4632-b47e-ed08593aff21","uuid":"215c02e4-2adc-45a0-8f73-7a36f32db679","tool_use_result":{"type":"create","filePath":"/Users/spy/mfautomations/repos/creation-station/reverse-search/synthetics/fixtures/jobs/ml-01-strong-staff.md","content":"---\n# Copyright 2026 VibeSpace LLC\n# Licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0\n#\n# JD Fixture: Strong match for synthetic-senior-ml\n# Contract: NUTRIENTS.md I.9 SyntheticJobFixture\n\ntarget_candidate: synthetic-senior-ml\nexpected_hot: true\nexpected_score_band: high\nsource: greenhouse\n---\n\n# Staff Machine Learning Engineer - LLM Infrastructure\n\n**Company:** Nexus AI\n**Location:** San Francisco, CA (Remote OK)\n**Salary:** $280,000 - $350,000 + equity\n\n## About Nexus AI\n\nNexus AI is building the next generation of AI infrastructure. Our platform powers some of the world's most demanding ML workloads, from training foundation models to serving billions of inference requests daily. Backed by $200M in Series C funding, we're growing rapidly and looking for exceptional talent.\n\n## The Role\n\nWe're looking for a Staff Machine Learning Engineer to lead technical direction for our LLM infrastructure team. You'll architect and build systems that train and serve large language models at massive scale, working alongside world-class researchers and engineers.\n\n## What You'll Do\n\n- Lead technical design for distributed training infrastructure supporting 1000+ GPU clusters\n- Architect efficient inference systems for LLMs with strict latency requirements\n- Drive adoption of best practices for MLOps, experiment tracking, and model versioning\n- Mentor a team of 5-8 ML engineers, fostering technical growth and excellence\n- Collaborate with research teams to productionize novel architectures\n- Publish technical blogs and represent the company at conferences\n- Contribute to open-source ML tooling and infrastructure projects\n\n## Requirements\n\n- 8+ years of experience in machine learning engineering\n- Deep expertise in PyTorch, distributed training (FSDP, DeepSpeed), and GPU optimization\n- Experience building production ML systems serving millions of users\n- Strong understanding of transformer architectures and attention mechanisms\n- Track record of leading technical initiatives and mentoring engineers\n- MS or PhD in Computer Science, Machine Learning, or related field\n- Published research in top-tier venues (NeurIPS, ICML, ICLR) preferred\n\n## Our Stack\n\n- Training: PyTorch, JAX, CUDA, Ray, Slurm\n- Inference: vLLM, TensorRT, Triton, Kubernetes\n- Infrastructure: AWS, GCP, custom on-prem clusters\n- Observability: Weights & Biases, Prometheus, Grafana\n\n## Benefits\n\n- Top-of-market compensation + generous equity\n- Premium health, dental, and vision coverage\n- $10,000 annual learning and conference budget\n- Flexible remote work with optional SF office access\n- Compute credits for personal research projects\n- Regular team offsites and company events\n\n## Why Join Us?\n\nYou'll work on some of the most challenging ML infrastructure problems in the industry, with access to massive compute resources and brilliant colleagues. If you're excited about pushing the boundaries of what's possible with large language models, we want to talk.\n","structuredPatch":[],"originalFile":null}}}
